    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     35,
     47
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link CharRange}. <p>Throughout this suite a {@link CharRange} is described by its factory method:</p> <ul> <li>{@code is(c)} / {@code isIn(start, end)} build a <em>normal</em> range that contains the listed characters.</li> <li>{@code isNot(c)} / {@code isNotIn(start, end)} build a <em>negated</em> range that contains every character <em>except</em> the listed ones.</li> <li>{@code isIn} / {@code isNotIn} automatically reorder reversed endpoints, so {@code a-e} equals {@code e-a}.</li> <li>{@link CharRange#toString()} renders a range as {@code start}, {@code start-end}, or with a leading {@code ^} when negated (for example {@code \"a\"}, {@code \"a-e\"}, {@code \"^a-e\"}).</li> </ul>"
   },
